Key difference:
- GEMM_1 maps thread (5,2) to a regular output patch at (16,40).
- GEMM_2 maps the same thread to a warp-rearranged output patch at (8,72).
- A-load indexing is similar, but C-tile ownership is not.
- This is one of the major readability/performance tradeoffs between the two kernels.
